    /**
     * ## Connect a device to a terminal
     *
     * Connect a device to a terminal instance. If the terminal has no device bound,
     * this will bind the provided `device_id` and generate a fresh API key token
     * (prefixed with `reservepay_`). If the terminal is already bound to the same
     * `device_id`, the previous key is revoked and a new one is issued.
     *
     * If the terminal is bound to a different device, an `ALREADY_CONNECTED` error
     * is returned.
     *
     * If the terminal is disabled, `NOT_ENABLED` is returned.
     *
     * If the terminal has no installation linked, `NOT_CONFIGURED` is returned.
     *
     * @throws org.webfunction.BadRequestException with code "ALREADY_CONNECTED" - The terminal is connected to another device.
     *
     * @throws org.webfunction.BadRequestException with code "INVALID_CHALLENGE" - The challenge is missing or does not match the terminal's current challenge.
     *
     * @throws org.webfunction.BadRequestException with code "NOT_FOUND" - Merchant or terminal could not be found.
     *
     * @throws org.webfunction.BadRequestException with code "NOT_ENABLED" - The terminal exists but is disabled; enable it before connecting a device.
     *
     * @throws org.webfunction.BadRequestException with code "NOT_CONFIGURED" - The terminal has no installation linked; assign an installation first.
     * @throws org.webfunction.UnexpectedStatusCodeException if the server responds with a non-200/400 status
     * @throws org.webfunction.JsonParseException if the response body isn't valid JSON
     */
